<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Kennedy returns two weeks after his first visit and is seen by Dr. Desai of endocrinology on the same day. He takes hydrocortisone 20 mg on waking and 10 mg at 2 pm and fludrocortisone half a tablet each morning, as the hospital prescribed, and has missed no doses. His energy is better than at discharge but fades by late afternoon. He craves salty food and feels lightheaded for a few seconds when he stands up quickly; he has not fainted. His appetite is good and he has gained a little weight. He has no nausea or abdominal pain. He started physical therapy last week and has done his exercises daily; his back still aches after long sitting and he wears the brace for the drive to work. He uses acetaminophen once or twice a day. He has practised with the trainer injection kit. He had his bone density scan this morning. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Replacement</td><td>Hydrocortisone 30 mg a day and fludrocortisone 0.05 mg a day since the hospital; no missed doses</td></tr><tr><td>Symptoms</td><td>Salt craving; brief lightheadedness on standing; afternoon tiredness</td></tr><tr><td>Weight</td><td>66.8 kg, up from 66.0</td></tr><tr><td>Back</td><td>Aches after sitting; first physical therapy session last week; acetaminophen once or twice a day</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

